From 052a670ef9a051a77689cafa9a0aa751c936fd44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 21:33:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03507/11362] [outer-loop] Constructed charger game:
 facing-aware omni GENERALISES to a new encoding + the UP facing

Operator: "build the constructed second charger game." Since no second real
charging-enemy game is reachable in the reproduced set, built an INDEPENDENT
simulator to test the facing-aware omni rule across encoding + the one facing
tu93 never exposed (UP).

- scripts/experiments/experiment_constructed_charger.py: GroundTruthChargerNav,
  own state+physics (NOT the model's is_lethal), non-tu93 palette (avatar 6/7,
  charger 11/13, wall 1, goal 12), step 5 (vs 6), an UP-facing charger, in a
  WALLED MAZE (corridors + detour bay, like tu93) so the avatar's 3x3 footprint
  never overlaps the charger -- closes the sprite-occlusion FN/FP an open field
  exposes (an open-field draft gave FP=4 from the avatar erasing the charger
  sprite -> facing unreadable).
- RESULT: omni fit from the constructed transitions detects the charger
  (learns charge_range=8), RECOVERS the UP facing (-1,0) from the centre-marker
  on the NEW sprite, scores FN=0/FP=0/win-path-unpruned vs a position-keyed BFS
  ground truth, and DEEPENS L0->L1 (reproduced) via the bay detour while a
  charger-blind frozen nav plans the straight path [4,4,4,4] and DIES at col 26.
- Adversarially verified before reporting: frozen nav *plans and dies* (not
  no-plan), omni's trail genuinely climbs to row 11 over the charger (uses the
  bay), the charger is genuinely detected as a hazard. tu93 L3 calibration
  re-run: still FN=0/FP=0 (model untouched by the env change). 8 unit tests pass.
- InducedNavWorldModel door detection now requires UBIQUITY (>=50% of moved
  gaps) so nav does not mis-pick a charger colour caught in a few gaps as the
  door -- needed for the new encoding; tu93 door detection unaffected (verified).
- HONEST scope: the constructed kill rule is the same physics FAMILY as omni's
  predicate with different constants -- a CONTROLLED encoding+UP-facing+layout
  generalization test, NOT an adversarial arbitrary-physics test; it complements
  the tu93 genuine-unseen-physics evidence.
- Also commits probe_chargers.py (the cross-game charger scan from the prior
  2nd-config milestone) and verification re-run artifacts.

Folded into docs/research-notes/hazard-aware-omni-second-config-2026-06-22.md.
mypy hook skipped (.venv/bin/mypy not installed); ruff format+check pass.
Conductor STOPPED (operator session choice).

